# Execution Plan — Task 143-001: Shell Injection Fix (tmux.ts)

## Objective
Prevent shell injection via taskId parameter in tmux.ts public functions.

## Steps

### 1. Create src/core/validators.ts
- `ValidationError` class extending Error with `code` property
- `validateTaskId(taskId: string)`: regex `/^[\w-]+$/`, max length 100, no null bytes
- Export both for use across codebase

### 2. Harden tmux.ts
- Import `validateTaskId` from validators.ts
- Add validation at entry of every public function that accepts taskId:
  - spawnWorker(), killWorker(), attachToWorkerPane(), sendKeys() (target param)
- Verify all spawnSync calls use array args (shell:false is default — already safe)
- Audit setupWatchWindow/createWatchLayout for path injection in string-interpolated commands

### 3. Tests
- tests/core/validators.test.ts: 7+ tests covering valid + 6 injection vectors
- tests/orchestra/tmux.test.ts: add validation rejection tests for public functions

### 4. Verify
- tsc --noEmit
- npx vitest run

## Files Modified
- src/core/validators.ts (NEW)
- src/orchestra/tmux.ts (MODIFIED)
- tests/core/validators.test.ts (NEW)
